@@ -1,7 +1,11 @@
-An HTTP server that routes each request by the method and target in its request line.
+An HTTP server that reads the request line, headers, and any Content-Length body before routing a request. Malformed or incomplete requests receive 400 Bad Request. Transfer-Encoding is not supported.
+
+`/echo` accepts any method and replies with plain text containing the method and path (for example, `POST /echo`). Existing GET routes are `/` and `/users/:userId/posts/:postId`.
 
 Run: `node server.js`
 
 Minimum Node.js version: 22
 
 Port: 8080
+
+Tests: `npm test`
